            <ArticleTitle>Bandaging society's wounds: a primary care perspective.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3122/jabfm.2010.01.090156</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Our patients often carry heavy burdens into the examination room. With our standard questioning, we medically divide and define them into recognizable parts, but as pieces of a whole they resist healing. Can we regain a vision of health beyond the isolated individual to one who might belong to a larger community of concern?</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
